  "integrationNotes": [
    "Dispatch rewards are cumulative within a session, so settleSession applies the difference from the persistent prior receipt.",
    "A session ledger number can be committed only once; lower ledger numbers are ignored, conflicting values at the same ledger fail, and closed sessions can never pay again.",
    "All profile mutations are protected by Web Locks and one localStorage setItem commit. No unsafe cross-tab localStorage lease fallback.",
    "In the user's Sea Cliff demonstration the balance moved from 1000 to 1240, 1480 and 1610 after two medical calls and a passenger transport. There was no periodic five-dollar balance increase in this session.",
    "The demonstrated medical job credited 10 for pickup, 30 for hospital handover and 200 cash / 100 points for completion. Passenger transport credited 10 for pickup, 20 on arrival and 100 cash / 50 points on completion. These are separate once-only ledger entries.",
    "Original intermediate awards and penalties, runtime price tables, and unresolved manual-only rules are documented by executable address in original-economy-evidence.json. Per-event cash and points are floored at zero when posted to the account."
  ]
}
